                     :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_]\n                                         :body (go rest-forms macro-env)}\n                              :operands [(discard-result\n                                           (compile-form head false\n                                                         (assoc env ::top-level true) macro-env))]}\n                       tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))]\n       (annotate-call-sites\n         (cond->> (go forms initial-macro-env)\n           (outcomes? env) top-boundary\n           ;; The two sibling closures share one frame: separate bindings would\n           ;; retain one extra helper environment in every closure a guest\n           ;; captures (the machine-data validation bound notices).\n           (outcomes? env) (#(u/app\n                               (u/lam '[dsg__admitted? dsg__intra_call] %)\n                               (u/sexp->uast\n                                 '(fn [dsg__candidate]\n                                    (if (data/map? dsg__candidate)\n                                      ;; A map is offered to the dereference\n                                      ;; only when the heap authenticates it\n                                      ;; (ruling of record, rule 2), as the\n                                      ;; descriptor projection treats a\n                                      ;; cell-backed callable\n                                      ;; (yang.antlr.md 8.10.2), whose entry\n                                      ;; lives in the cell contents. The\n                                      ;; issued format (`:type :cell-ref`,\n                                      ;; `:id`, `:seal`, no other entries, a\n                                      ;; 64-character string seal) is only\n                                      ;; the pre-filter for WHEN to ask;\n                                      ;; `cell/authentic?` — the issuer's\n                                      ;; own heap+seal answer — decides, so\n                                      ;; any `:id` spelling may be asked\n                                      ;; about and the r4 heap-id-language\n                                      ;; discriminator is retired. A shape\n                                      ;; the heap does not authenticate is\n                                      ;; data: it falls to the witness\n                                      ;; branch and, entryless, is no more\n                                      ;; admitted than any other source map,\n                                      ;; so its invocation stays ordinary\n                                      ;; map data. An authenticated\n                                      ;; reference dereferences; an\n                                      ;; authenticated cell whose contents\n                                      ;; carry no callable entry is not\n                                      ;; admitted (authentication is not\n                                      ;; authorization, rule 3), and the\n                                      ;; call-site routing that consulted\n                                      ;; here refuses it as not-callable.\n                                      (let [dsg__cell-ref?\n                                            (if (dsg__equal\n                                                  (dsg__get dsg__candidate :type)\n                                                  :cell-ref)\n                                              (if (data/contains? dsg__candidate\n                                                                  :id)\n                                                (if (data/contains? dsg__candidate\n                                                                    :seal)\n                                                  (if (dsg__equal\n                                                        (data/count dsg__candidate)\n                                                        3)\n                                                    (if (data/string?\n                                                          (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n                                                                    :seal))\n                                                      (if (dsg__equal\n                                                            (data/str-length\n                                                              (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n                                                                        :seal))\n                                                            64)\n                                                        true\n                                                        false)\n                                                      false)\n                                                    false)\n                                                  false)\n                                                false)\n                                              false)]\n                                        (if dsg__cell-ref?\n                                          (if (cell/authentic? dsg__candidate)\n                                            (let [dsg__descriptor\n                                                  (cell/get dsg__candidate)\n                                                  dsg__entry\n                                                  (dsg__get dsg__descriptor\n                                                            :yang.call/entry)]\n                                              (data/callable? dsg__entry))\n                                            false)\n                                          (let [dsg__entry\n                                                (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n                                                          :yang.call/entry)\n                                                dsg__witness\n                                                (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n                                                          :clj/admission)]\n                                            (if (data/callable? dsg__entry)\n                                              (if (data/callable? dsg__witness)\n                                                (dsg__equal\n                                                  dsg__witness\n                                                  (dsg__make_admission\n                                                    (dsg__assoc dsg__candidate\n                                                                :clj/admission\n                                                                nil)))\n                                                false)\n                                              false))))\n                                      false)))\n                               ;; The intra-unit dispatcher: resolve the unit's public entry,\n                               ;; apply it with the compiler's token packet [token args] - one\n                               ;; variadic conj and one application, no record construction.\n                               ;; Non-map callees refuse.\n                               (u/sexp->uast\n                                 (list 'fn '[dsg__callee dsg__args]\n                                       (list 'if '(data/map? dsg__callee)\n                                             (list (list (if (contains? (::defined env) 'get)\n                                                           'dsg__get\n                                                           'get)\n                                                         'dsg__callee\n                                                         :yang.call/entry)\n                                                   (list 'conj '[]\n                                                         'dsg__call_token\n                                                         'dsg__args))\n                                             '(clj/raise\n                                                (yang.call/condition\n                                                  :yang.call/not-callable\n                                                  (dsg__assoc {} :yang.call/callee dsg__callee))))))))\n           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__make_entry (call-entry))\n           (outcomes? env) (u/let1\n                             'dsg__make_admission\n                             (u/sexp->uast\n                               '(fn [dsg__descriptor]\n                                  (fn [dsg__candidate]\n                                    (if (data/callable? dsg__call_token)\n                                      (dsg__get dsg__descriptor :yang.call/entry)\n                                      nil)))))\n           ;; The exception accessors and the continuation family. The\n           ;; `dsg__ex_message`/`dsg__ex_data` accessors read the portable\n           ;; ex-info map; the continuation family (`clj/try`, `clj/throw`,\n           ;; `clj/raise`, ...) is the port's `%capture` handler-stack scheme,\n           ;; emitted inline (the linked runtime binds the same family from the\n           ;; prelude). Its capture-sensitive primitives are the `dsg__*`\n           ;; names bound outside it.\n           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__ex_message\n                                   (u/sexp->uast ex-message-form))\n           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__ex_data\n                                   (u/sexp->uast ex-data-form))\n           (outcomes? env) (u/then\n                             (discard-result continuation-uast))\n           (outcomes? env) (u/then\n                             (discard-result\n                               (u/app (u/lam '[get = assoc empty?] call/uast)\n                                      (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n                                      (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/v 'dsg__empty))))\n           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__call_token (u/lam [] (u/lit nil)))\n           ;; Guest closures keep captured environments portable: binding host\n           ;; primitive values here would make UCF machine-data validation fail.\n           ;; These helpers cover generated map lookups/writes and comparisons;\n           ;; conj/vec are already protected by the convention's binder checks.\n           ;; Evaluate siblings outside each other's bindings to avoid retaining\n           ;; a chain of redundant helper environments.\n           (outcomes? env) (#(u/app\n                               (u/lam '[dsg__get dsg__equal dsg__assoc dsg__empty] %)\n                               (if (contains? (::defined env) 'get)\n                                 (u/sexp->uast\n                                   '(fn [m k]\n                                      (if (data/map? m)\n                                        (let [find (fn [self entries]\n                                                     (if (data/content= 0 (data/count entries))\n                                                       nil\n                                                       (let [pair (data/nth entries 0)]\n                                                         (if (data/content= k (data/nth pair 0))\n                                                           (data/nth pair 1)\n                                                           (self self (data/subvec entries 1))))))]\n                                          (find find (vec m)))\n                                        nil)))\n                   :consumer\n                   vm/value)]\n    (testing \"a raised condition without a qualified reason still takes the\n              §8.10.7 shape: :yang.call/thrown carrying the original value\"\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok\n              {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n               :yang.call/value {:yin.k/message \"Clojure functions do not accept named arguments\"\n                                 :yin.k/data {:yang.call/named [[\"x\" 1]]}}}]\n             result)))\n    (testing \"a condition with a qualified reason is forwarded unchanged\"\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok :yang.call/not-callable]\n             (run-profile-outcome\n               '[(let [condition (yang.call/invoke 5 [21] [] profile-raise)]\n                   (get condition :yang.call/reason))]))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The exception track, Clojure round R3: protocol failures retain and\n;; forward the complete condition (ruling v2, §R3; design §8.10.7)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(declare run-cell-program)\n(declare run-library library-opts)\n\n\n(defn- cell-entry-node\n  [condition]\n  (u/app (u/v 'cell/new)\n         (u/app (u/v 'assoc) (u/lit {})\n                (u/lit :yang.call/entry)\n                (u/lam ['invocation]\n                       (u/app (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v 'invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/raise))\n                              (u/lit condition))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-exception-r3-protocol-condition-forwarded-unchanged\n  (testing \"a protocol failure delivered to the guest's own raise continuation\n            is caught and rethrown unchanged: the complete original condition,\n            qualified reason AND plain evidence, with no :yang.call/thrown\n            wrapper (ruling R3: the call site no longer reclassifies)\"\n    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\n      (doseq [[reason evidence]\n              [[:yang.call/not-callable {:yang.call/callee 5}]\n               [:yang.call/invalid-invocation {:yang.call/callee :target}]\n               [:yang.call/unsupported-binding\n                {:yang.call/binding-profile :contract/unsupported}]]]\n        (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yang.call/reason reason :yang.call/data evidence}]\n               (run-cell-program\n                 '[(defn receive\n                     [f]\n                     (try (f) (catch Exception e (throw e))))\n                   (receive marker-operand)]\n                 (cell-entry-node {:yang.call/reason reason :yang.call/data evidence})\n                 lane))\n            (str lane \" \" reason \" forwards the condition the convention built, with\n                 its evidence, unchanged\")))))\n  (testing \"(A): an ordinary thrown condition delivers its payload raw;\n            evidence beyond `:yang.call/value` is not retained across a\n            call site - the wire condition is reconstructible from the\n            payload as a fresh thrown condition at a public entry\"\n    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\n      (let [condition {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n                       :yang.call/value {:foreign/payload :identity}\n                       :yang.call/data {:complete [:extra :evidence]}}]\n        (is (= [:yin.k/error {:foreign/payload :identity}]\n               (run-cell-program\n                 '[(defn run\n                     [f]\n                     (f))\n                   (run marker-operand)]\n                 (cell-entry-node condition)\ncollab/yang-python/1792200000000-reviewer-ts-php-designs.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:24:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba collab/1792197000000-architect-yang-ts-php-designs.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md | sed -n '305,385p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   305\\t| Group | Arms | Lowering |\\n   306\\t|---|---|---|\\n   307\\t| Output | `echo`, `print`, `inlineHtml`, `printf`/`sprintf`/`number_format` (prelude) | `php/echo` appends to the output-buffer stack |\\n   308\\t| Variables | `$x`, `$this`, `$GLOBALS[...]`, superglobals, `$$x` (dynamic profile), list()/[] destructuring with keys and refs | `php/local-get`/`cell/get` through the marker deref; writes `php/assign` (deref-aware) |\\n   309\\t| Operators | arithmetic (overflow to float), string `.`, `.=`, comparison (`==`, `===`, `<=>`, `<` with the juggling table), logical (`&&`, `and` precedence difference is the grammar's), `??`, `??=`, ternary and short ternary, bitwise (int only; on strings bytewise), casts `(int)`/`(string)`/`(array)`/`(object)`/`(bool)`/`(float)`, `instanceof`, `clone`, `new`, error-suppression `@` (diagnostics muted for the expression), increment/decrement (string and null rules), `print` as expression | `php/*` applications |\\n   310\\t| Arrays | literals with keys/spread/refs, `$a[k]`, `$a[]`, nested writes, `unset($a[k])`, `isset`/`empty`, `foreach` by value, by key, by reference, with `list` | path updates on the value in the cell; `php/array-*` |\\n   311\\t| Strings | single-quoted, double-quoted with interpolation (`$x`, `{$x->y}`, `${x}`, `$a[k]`), heredoc/nowdoc (indentation removal rule of 7.3), escape sequences incl. `\\\\u{...}` as UTF-8 bytes | `php/str-concat` of parts; each part `php/to-string` |\\n   312\\t| Control | if/elseif/else, alternative syntax (`if: endif;`), while/do/for (comma expressions), switch (loose `==`, fallthrough, `continue` inside switch acts as `break` with the 7.3 warning), `break n`/`continue n`, `match`, `return`, `goto` refused | loops self-applied `:loop` lambdas; multi-level escapes index the `:loop` stack |\\n   313\\t| Functions | declarations (hoisted or in place), closures with `use`, arrow fns, defaults, by-ref params, variadics, named args, nullable/union type declarations with coercion or `TypeError`, return types, `static` vars, `global`, first-class callable `f(...)`, callables | `php/make-function name spec code statics`; calls `php/call callee args named-args class-ctx` |\\n   314\\t| Classes | class/abstract/final/readonly, properties (typed, defaults, static), constants (`final`, visibility), methods, constructors with promotion, `static`/`self`/`parent`, interfaces, traits (`use`, `insteadof`, `as`), enums (pure and backed), attributes (parsed, stored as data on the descriptor for `ReflectionAttribute` later, no runtime effect), magic methods, `__toString` in string contexts, `instanceof` | `php/declare-class` at the declaration point into the class table; traits copied there |\\n   315\\t| Exceptions | try/catch/finally, multi-catch, throw expression, rethrow | handler stack with `php/raise`; `finally` via `php/try-finally` |\\n   316\\t| Generators | yield, yield key => value, yield from, send/throw/getReturn | C2 core under `php/gen-*` |\\n   317\\t| Modules | `include`/`require`/`_once`, `namespace`, `use`, `declare(strict_types)`, `declare(ticks)` | B6 |\\n   318\\t| Refused | goto, return by reference, eval (until its slice), `$$` outside the dynamic profile slice, `__halt_compiler`, `declare(encoding)`, `list()` with references nested beyond one level in Phase 3 | `:yang.php/unsupported {:construct}` |\\n   319\\t\\n   320\\t**Prelude inventory**, module `php` (reserved), hook prelude `phpsp`; `php/init!` builds the class table with the builtin classes and interfaces (`stdClass`, `Closure`, `Generator`, `ArrayObject` deferred, `Traversable`, `Iterator`, `IteratorAggregate`, `ArrayAccess`, `Countable`, `Stringable`, `JsonSerializable`, `UnitEnum`/`BackedEnum`, the `Throwable` hierarchy), the function table with the supported builtins, `$GLOBALS` from the request record, the output-buffer stack, the error-handler cell, the included-files dict, and flips `php.rt/state` to `:php/ready`.\\n   321\\t\\n   322\\t| Area | Supported core (Phase 3) | Est. lines |\\n   323\\t|---|---|---|\\n   324\\t| Type juggling | `to-int`, `to-float`, `to-string` (precision 14), `to-bool`, `to-array`, numeric-string classification, `==`/`<=>`/`===` tables, `gettype`, `is_*`, `intval`/`floatval`/`strval`/`boolval`/`settype`, `var_dump`/`print_r`/`var_export` text (serialize_precision -1, the `#n` object ids, indentation rules) | 700 |\\n   325\\t| Arrays | `count`, `array_keys/values/merge/merge_recursive/combine/flip/slice/splice/map/filter/reduce/walk/search/key_exists/in_array/unique/reverse/sum/product/fill/fill_keys/pad/chunk/column/diff/intersect(+_key/_assoc)/push/pop/shift/unshift/key_first/key_last/is_list`, `sort/rsort/usort/uasort/uksort/ksort/krsort/asort/arsort` (stable since 8.0, flags subset), `range`, `compact`/`extract` (dynamic profile), `list`, `implode`/`explode`/`str_split`, `array_key_exists`, `iterator_to_array`, `current/key/next/reset/end/prev` (the internal pointer is a per-array-value position in the cell content) | 900 |\\n   326\\t| Strings (byte strings) | `strlen`, `substr`, `strpos/stripos/strrpos`, `str_replace/str_ireplace`, `str_contains/starts_with/ends_with`, `trim/ltrim/rtrim`, `strtolower/strtoupper/ucfirst/ucwords/lcfirst` (ASCII, PHP 8 locale-insensitive), `str_repeat/str_pad/strrev/strcmp/strcasecmp/strncmp/strstr/strrchr/substr_count/wordwrap/nl2br/htmlspecialchars/html_entity_decode (basic)/addslashes/stripslashes/chunk_split`, `sprintf/printf/vsprintf/number_format`, `ord/chr/bin2hex/hex2bin/dechex/hexdec/decbin/bindec/octdec/decoct/base_convert`, `md5/sha1/crc32/hash('sha256')` via `data`/BLAKE3-era pure kernels only if present, else refused, `json_encode/json_decode` (flags subset, `JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR`, pretty print), `serialize/unserialize` deferred, `preg_*` refused | 900 |\\n   327\\t| Math | `abs/ceil/floor/round` (PHP's pre-rounding rule)/`intdiv/fmod/pow/sqrt/min/max/array_sum`, `PHP_INT_MAX/MIN/SIZE`, `PHP_FLOAT_*`, `M_PI`, `is_nan/is_finite/is_infinite`, `rand/mt_rand/random_int` as effects | 250 |\\n   328\\t| Functions and classes | call binding (positional, named, variadic, by-ref, defaults, type coercion/`TypeError`, `ArgumentCountError`), `func_get_args`, `call_user_func(_array)`, `is_callable`, `function_exists`, class table ops, `get_class`, `get_parent_class`, `method_exists`, `property_exists`, `class_exists`, `get_object_vars`, `spl_object_id`, visibility checks, magic dispatch, `Closure::bind/fromCallable/call`, enums `cases/from/tryFrom` | 700 |\\n   329\\t| Control and errors | handler stack (the Python pattern), `php/raise`, `finally`, escapes with levels, `Throwable` classes with `getMessage/getCode/getPrevious/getTrace (empty)/getLine (derived at the boundary)`, `set_error_handler/restore_error_handler/set_exception_handler/trigger_error/error_reporting`, warning emission `php/warn` | 350 |\\n   330\\t| Generators and iteration | C2 core under `php/`, `Iterator` protocol, `foreach` driver, `yield from` over arrays and generators | 300 |\\n   331\\t| Request and output | `$_*` construction, `php/echo`, `ob_*` stack, `header/headers_sent/http_response_code/setcookie`, `exit`, `php_sapi_name` (\\\"cli\\\" or \\\"yin-http\\\" pinned), `getenv` from the record only, `PHP_EOL`, `PHP_VERSION` pinned, `error_log` as an effect | 300 |\\n   332\\t| Module runtime | `include/require/_once`, included-files dict, autoload class map, `define/constant/defined`, namespaces lookup | 250 |\\n   333\\t\\n   334\\tRefusal posture: a builtin outside the supported core is `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` at lowering (warning) and `Error: Call to undefined function` at run time; an extension surface is bound per ADR 0004 as its own slice with an effect schema and an interpreter; nothing is stubbed to return success.\\n   335\\t\\n   336\\t## B5. Value encoding and the paradigm rows finalized\\n   337\\t\\n   338\\t| PHP type | Representation |\\n   339\\t|---|---|\\n   340\\t| int | exact integer within `[-2^63, 2^63-1]` (C3 carriers; on JS a value past 2^53 is a `BigInt` carrier); overflow of an operation demotes to float |\\n   341\\t| float | Jing float64 content (carrier on JS); one NaN; `-0.0` preserved; `INF` |\\n   342\\t| string | **byte string**: a host string whose every char is one byte 0..255 (latin-1 carrier of the bytes); source literals contribute their UTF-8 bytes; `strlen` is bytes; output writes the bytes raw; `mb_*` is a separate slice over this representation. Owner decision B8.2 states the alternative. |\\n   343\\t| bool | host boolean |\\n   344\\t| null | `:php/null` |\\n   345\\t| array | persistent ordered-map value in the holder's cell or slot (B1) |\\n   346\\t| object | cell ref (handle); `clone` allocates a fresh cell |\\n   347\\t| reference | `{:php/ref c}` marker in a variable cell, array slot or property slot |\\n   348\\t| closure | object cell of class `Closure` holding the code closure, bound `$this`, scope class and `use`d values or markers |\\n   349\\t| enum case | singleton object cell per case |\\n   350\\t| resource | opaque handle data from a bound surface (`{:php/resource kind id}`), none in Phase 3 |\\n   351\\t| callable | string, `[class-or-obj, name]` array, or `Closure`; resolved at call |\\n   352\\t\\n   353\\t```text\\n   354\\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------+------------+\\n   355\\t| Paradigm                   | Universal AST target                             | Reference  |\\n   356\\t+============================+==================================================+============+\\n   357\\t| Value-copy ordered maps    | Arrays are persistent ordered-map values in      | PHP        |\\n   358\\t| with reference slots and   | cells (O(1) copy); references are markers in     |            |\\n   359\\t| request scope (new row,    | slots; objects are cell handles; locals are      |            |\\n   360\\t| finalizing D5)             | cells, dynamic-scope functions a heap symbol     |            |\\n   361\\t|                            | table; the global scope is the $GLOBALS dict; a  |            |\\n   362\\t|                            | request is one task reading one request record   |            |\\n   363\\t|                            | and appending ordered output records; warnings   |            |\\n   364\\t|                            | are diagnostic records, fatals are throws        |            |\\n   365\\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------+------------+\\n   366\\t| PHP number model           | int = exact integer bounded at 2^63 with overflow|            |\\n   367\\t|                            | to float (detected by exact promotion, demoted   |            |\\n   368\\t|                            | by rule); float = float64 content (carrier on    |            |\\n   369\\t|                            | JS); echo at precision 14, var_dump shortest;    |            |\\n   370\\t|                            | array keys coerce int-like strings and floats to |            |\\n   371\\t|                            | int                                              |            |\\n   372\\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------+------------+\\n   373\\t| Class-based OO (existing   | Class descriptors in cells, traits copied at     | PHP (with  |\\n   374\\t| row, PHP entry qualified)  | declaration, interfaces as dispatch contracts,   | Java,      |\\n   375\\t|                            | runtime visibility against a class context       | Python)    |\\n   376\\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------+------------+\\n   377\\t```\\n   378\\t\\n   379\\t## B6. include/require over the linker, safepoints, diagnostics, the corpus\\n   380\\t\\n   381\\t- **Units and names**: a PHP file compiled as unit `src/lib/util.php` becomes linker module `phpm.src$lib$util` (injective mangling of the normalized relative path; `/` and `.` to `$`-escapes); shape as Python's: `(do (require 'php) (yin/def spec {:path \\\"src/lib/util.php\\\" :strict-types 0}) (yin/def body (fn [%scope %ctx] ...)))`. `include 'x.php'` with a **literal** path (after constant folding of `__DIR__ . '/x.php'`, which the lowering performs since `__DIR__` is the unit's declared path, not a filesystem fact) lowers to the I4-a statement-time delivery thunk; the body runs in the **including scope** (passing the including scope's symbol table, which is why an including function is on the dynamic profile; at top level it is `$GLOBALS`); the body's `return` value is the expression's value, else `1`. `_once` consults the included-files dict. A missing `include` is `Warning` plus `false`; a missing `require` is `Error` (PHP 8: `Error`, fatal). Computed paths are a diagnostic (ruling 10's literal-name restriction; a published literal path map can later interpret them). Conditional declarations inside included files execute in place, as PHP does. Cycles of `include` are a runtime matter (the included-files dict), not a linker cycle: static `include` edges are pinned in `:requires` only for delivery, and SCC publication handles mutual pins. **Autoload**: `spl_autoload_register` with a guest callable is supported only when the composition also publishes a literal **class map** (class name to unit) as part of the unit set; the autoloader then runs on a class miss and may `require` only literal paths in that map. Composer's generated class map is admissible as data; its filesystem resolution is not.\\n   382\\t- **Namespaces** are compile-time; nothing links per namespace.\\n   383\\t- **Safepoints**: `:loop` and `:call` for signals (`pcntl_signal` handlers run at hooks via `stream/poll!` on a signal stream, `pcntl_async_signals` is the default and only mode) and for recursion depth if a composition wants a bound (PHP has none; default off); `:line` under a ticks profile for `declare(ticks=N)` and `register_tick_function`. `max_execution_time` and `set_time_limit` are wall-clock in PHP, so nondeterministic: the profile offers a deterministic **safepoint-count budget** instead, raising the fatal with PHP's text; a recorded departure. No thread switches: PHP is single-threaded; one request is one task.\\n   384\\t- **Diagnostics**: compile-time `:yang.php/syntax`, `:yang.php/unsupported`, `:yang.php/not-php`, `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` (warning), `:yang.php/compile-error` for PHP's compile-time fatals (redeclared function in one unit, `break 0`, duplicate parameter, `$this` reassignment); runtime guest warnings on the guest-diagnostics stream; fatals as `Error` throws; uncaught text pinned.\\n   385\\t- **Differential corpus**: pinned PHP 8.3.x CLI with the pinned ini; stdout plus the diagnostics stream rendered in PHP's `Warning: ... in <unit> on line N` form with the path replaced by the unit name and the line derived from the side table (owner decision 2 of 8.5.1 reused) compared against PHP's stderr with paths normalized. Groups: juggling (every `==` pair of the PHP 8 table, numeric strings, arithmetic warnings/`TypeError`), arrays (key coercion, order, next index after unset, copy-on-write observable through references, nested writes, `foreach` by reference pitfalls, sort stability), references (`&` in all five positions, `global`, `static`), strings (bytes, interpolation forms, heredoc indentation, `precision=14` output, `var_dump` text), functions (named args, by-ref, defaults, variadics, type coercion vs `strict_types`), classes (traits precedence, visibility, static/late static binding, magic methods, readonly errors, enums, `match`), exceptions (finally ordering, multi-catch, `Error` hierarchy), generators, request (superglobals from a fixture record, headers after output warning, `ob_*`), inclusion (`_once`, return values, scope sharing, missing include warning vs require error), safepoints (ticks counting, signal at a hook).\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-python/1792200000000-reviewer-ts-php-designs.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:39:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_19\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n 'float-digits|defn.*float' src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc; rg -n 'string|utf|surrogate|UTF' src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc | head -45; rg -n 'binders|:lambda|params|:variable' src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc | head -40; sed -n '2155,2291p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc; rg -n 'jobs|JavaScript|completion|shared|atomic|cell/swap' docs/design/yang.antlr.md\\\"\",\"aggre