                  (+ d 2))]))\\n  1019\\t    :else (let [[_ n den] (exact x)]\\n  1020\\t            (deep! (inc d) :unsupported-value)\\n  1238\\t  each captured continuation at most once. Section 8.5.3 records the C2\\n  1239\\t  design that realizes this.\\n  1240\\t\\n  1241\\tTruthiness, arbitrary-precision integers, division, equality, attribute\\n  1242\\tlookup, descriptors, and iteration belong to the Python runtime profile.\\n  1243\\tThe Python value encoding tags floats on every host, since JavaScript\\n  1244\\tcannot distinguish `2` from `2.0` and ints are the common case (Python\\n  1245\\tmappability ruling, owner decision 3); `print(4/2)` belongs in the Node\\n  1246\\tparity set. Integers stay untagged at every magnitude; section 8.5.4\\n  1247\\trecords the C3 integer rulings.\\n  1248\\t\\n  1249\\tGenerator support is incomplete until `send`, `throw`, `close`, cleanup,\\n  1250\\tand suspension are tested. It is not established by parsing `yield`.\\n  1251\\t\\n  1860\\t|        | user-defined iterator classes.                                      |\\n  1861\\t+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n  1862\\t```\\n  1863\\t\\n  1864\\tThe cross-ruling strengthens acceptance:\\n  1865\\t\\n  1866\\t- Every slice runs on all four evaluators on JVM, Node, and Dart;\\n  1867\\t  \\\"wherever the parity lane runs\\\" does not support a portability claim.\\n  1868\\t  Expected output for source programs is CPython 3.9.6's.\\n  1869\\t- Ruling 1: nested generators, different resuming callers, and\\n  1870\\t  suspension during exception unwinding.\\n  1871\\t- Ruling 2: flags become collectible when unreachable, not necessarily\\n  1872\\t  right after re-entry, so reachable heap is measured after repeated\\n  1873\\t  suspension and collection.\\n  1874\\t- Ruling 4: short-circuiting and side effects, not only PEP 479.\\n  1875\\t- Ruling 7: the complete reachable continuation and heap graph across\\n  1876\\