-------------------------------------------------+\\n  2122\\t| S5     | Numeric dict and set keys and guest hashes.                         |\\n  2123\\t+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n  2124\\t| S6     | Heap and portability: collection, pinning, scalar UCF round trips,  |\\n  2125\\t|        | honest refusal of cell lift and raw transport.                      |\\n  2126\\t+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n  2127\\t| S7     | Integration gate over the full C1 and C3 corpus, profile mismatch,  |\\n  2128\\t|        | and resource-limit fixtures.                                        |\\n  2129\\t+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n  2130\\t```\\n  2131\\t\\n  2132\\tC3 is complete only with (ruling 14):\\n  2133\\t\\n  2134\\t- All four VMs on JVM, Node, and Dart VM, twelve lanes; Dart compiled to\\n  2680\\t\\n  2681\\tThe runtime/prelude profile pins language semantics as explicit data.\\n  2682\\tFor Python under C3 it names the integer and binary64 conversion\\n  2683\\tsemantics, the numeric hash modulus, the integer-text conversion\\n  2684\\tpolicy, the admitted numeric limits, and the required pure modules and\\n  2685\\tboundary adapters; resource checks use portable quantities such as bit\\n  2686\\tlengths and digit counts, never host object sizes or available memory\\n  2687\\t(section 8.5.4). A prelude that grows, as C2's does, changes every\\n  2688\\tbundled unit's address and is a prelude-profile bump.\\n  2689\\t\\n  2690\\tCross-host content-address claims remain conditional on the canonical\\n  2691\\tencoding actually used. The disclosed `dao.jing` encoding residuals\\n  2692\\trequire explicit conformance tests and profile restrictions or fixes;\\n  2693\\tthis document does not silently replace its addressing scheme.\\n  2694\\t\\n  2695\\t---\\n  2696\\t\\n  2697\\t## 12. Phased roadmap\\n  2698\