ns do not accept named arguments\\\"\\n                                 :yin.k/data {:yang.call/named [[\\\"x\\\" 1]]}}}]\\n             result)))\\n    (testing \\\"a condition with a qualified reason is forwarded unchanged\\\"\\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok :yang.call/not-callable]\\n             (run-profile-outcome\\n               '[(let [condition (yang.call/invoke 5 [21] [] profile-raise)]\\n                   (get condition :yang.call/reason))]))))))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; The exception track, Clojure round R3: protocol failures retain and\\n;; forward the complete condition (ruling v2, §R3; design §8.10.7)\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n(declare run-cell-program)\\n(declare run-library library-opts)\\n\\n\\n(defn- cell-entry-node\\n  [condition]\\n  (u/app (u/v 'cell/new)\\n         (u/app (u/v 'assoc) (u/lit {})\\n                (u/lit :yang.call/entry)\\n                (u/lam ['invocation]\\n                       (u/app (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v 'invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/raise))\\n                              (u/lit condition))))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest test-exception-r3-protocol-condition-forwarded-unchanged\\n  (testing \\\"a protocol failure delivered to the guest's own raise continuation\\n            is caught and rethrown unchanged: the complete original condition,\\n            qualified reason AND plain evidence, with no :yang.call/thrown\\n            wrapper (ruling R3: the call site no longer reclassifies)\\\"\\n    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\\n      (doseq [[reason evidence]\\n              [[:yang.call/not-callable {:yang.call/callee 5}]\\n               [:yang.call/invalid-invocation {:yang.call/callee :target}]\\n               [:yang.call/unsupported-binding\\n                {:yang.call/binding-profile :contract/unsupported}]]]\\n        (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yang.call/reason reason :yang.call/data evidence}]\\n               (run-cell-program\\n                 '[(defn receive\\n                     [f]\\n                     (try (f) (catch Exception e (throw e))))\\n                   (receive marker-operand)]\\n                 (cell-entry-node {:yang.call/reason reason :yang.call/data evidence})\\n                 lane))\\n            (str lane \\\" \\\" reason \\\" forwards the condition the convention built, with\\n                 its evidence, unchanged\\\")))))\\n  (testing \\\"(A): an ordinary thrown condition delivers its payload raw;\\n            evidence beyond `:yang.call/value` is not retained across a\\n            call site - the wire condition is reconstructible from the\\n            payload as a fresh thrown condition at a public entry\\\"\\n    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\\n      (let [condition {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\\n                       :yang.call/value {:foreign/payload :identity}\\n                       :yang.call/data {:complete [:extra :evidence]}}]\\n        (is (= [:yin.k/error {:foreign/payload :identity}]\\n               (run-cell-program\\n                 '[(defn run\\n                     [f]\\n                     (f))\\n                   (run marker-operand)]\\n                 (cell-entry-node condition)\\ncollab/yang-python/1792200000000-reviewer-ts-php-designs.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:24:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba collab/1792197000000-architect-yang-ts-php-designs.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md | sed -n '305,385p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"   305\\\\t| Group | Arms | Lowering |\\\\n   306\\\\t|---|---|---|\\\\n   307\\\\t| Output | `echo`, `print`, `inlineHtml`, `printf`/`sprintf`/`number_format` (prelude) | `php/echo` appends to the output-buffer stack |\\\\n   308\\\\t| Variables | `$x`, `$this`, `$GLOBALS[...]`, superglobals, `$$x` (dynamic profile), list()/[] destructuring with keys and refs | `php/local-get`/`cell/get` through the marker deref; writes `php/assign` (deref-aware) |\\\\n   309\\\\t| Operators | arithmetic (overflow to float), string `.`, `.=`, comparison (`==`, `===`, `<=>`, `<` with the juggling table), logical (`&&`, `and` precedence difference is the grammar's), `??`, `??=`, ternary and short ternary, bitwise (int only; on strings bytewise), casts `(int)`/`(string)`/`(array)`/`(object)`/`(bool)`/`(float)`, `instanceof`, `clone`, `new`, error-suppression `@` (diagnostics muted for the expression), increment/decrement (string and null rules), `print` as expression | `php/*` applications |\\\\n   310\\\\t| Arrays | literals with keys/spread/refs, `$a[k]`, `$a[]`, nested writes, `unset($a[k])`, `isset`/`empty`, `foreach` by value, by key, by reference, with `list` | path updates on the value in the cell; `php/array-*` |\\\\n   311\\\\t| Strings | single-quoted, double-quoted with interpolation (`$x`, `{$x->y}`, `${x}`, `$a[k]`), heredoc/nowdoc (indentation removal rule of 7.3), escape sequences incl. `\\\\\\\\u{...}` as UTF-8 bytes | `php/str-concat` of parts; each part `php/to-string` |\\\\n   312\\\\t| Control | if/elseif/else, alternative syntax (`if: endif;`), while/do/for (comma expressions), switch (loose `==`, fallthrough, `continue` inside switch acts as `break` with the 7.3 warning), `break n`/`continue n`, `match`, `return`, `goto` refused | loops self-applied `:loop` lambdas; multi-level escapes index the `:loop` stack |\\\\n   313\\\\t| Functions | declarations (hoisted or in place), closures with `use`, arrow fns, defaults, by-ref params, variadics, named args, nullable/union type declarations with coercion or `TypeError`, return types, `static` vars, `global`, first-class callable `f(...)`, callables | `php/make-function name spec code statics`; calls `php/call callee args named-args class-ctx` |\\\\n   314\\\\t| Classes | class/abstract/final/readonly, properties (typed, defaults, static), constants (`final`, visibility), methods, constructors with promotion, `static`/`self`/`parent`, interfaces, traits (`use`, `insteadof`, `as`), enums (pure and backed), attributes (parsed, stored as data on the descriptor for `ReflectionAttribute` later, no runtime effect), magic methods, `__toString` in string contexts, `instanceof` | `php/declare-class` at the declaration point into the class table; traits copied there |\\\\n   315\\\\t| Exceptions | try/catch/finally, multi-catch, throw expression, rethrow | handler stack with `php/raise`; `finally` via `php/try-finally` |\\\\n   316\\\\t| Generators | yield, yield key => value, yield from, send/throw/getReturn | C2 core under `php/gen-*` |\\\\n   317\\\\t| Modules | `include`/`require`/`_once`, `namespace`, `use`, `declare(strict_types)`, `declare(ticks)` | B6 |\\\\n   318\\\\t| Refused | goto, return by reference, eval (until its slice), `$$` outside the dynamic profile slice, `__halt_compiler`, `declare(encoding)`, `list()` with references nested beyond one level in Phase 3 | `:yang.php/unsupported {:construct}` |\\\\n   319\\\\t\\\\n   320\\\\t**Prelude inventory**, module `php` (reserved), hook prelude `phpsp`; `php/init!` builds the class table with the builtin classes and interfaces (`stdClass`, `Closure`, `Generator`, `ArrayObject` deferred, `Traversable`, `Iterator`, `IteratorAggregate`, `ArrayAccess`, `Countable`, `Stringable`, `JsonSerializable`, `UnitEnum`/`BackedEnum`, the `Throwable` hierarchy), the function table with the supported builtins, `$GLOBALS` from the request record, the output-buffer stack, the error-handler cell, the included-files dict, and flips `php.rt/state` to `:php/ready`.\\\\n   321\\\\t\\\\n   322\\\\t| Area | Supported core (Phase 3) | Est. lines |\\\\n   323\\\\t|---|---|---|\\\\n   324\\\\t| Type juggling | `to-int`, `to-float`, `to-string` (precision 14), `to-bool`, `to-array`, numeric-string classification, `==`/`<=>`/`===` tables, `gettype`, `is_*`, `intval`/`floatval`/`strval`/`boolval`/`settype`, `var_dump`/`print_r`/`var_export` text (serialize_precision -1, the `#n` object ids, indentation rules) | 700 |\\\\n   325\\\\t| Arrays | `count`, `array_keys/values/merge/merge_recursive/combine/flip/slice/splice/map/filter/reduce/walk/search/key_exists/in_array/unique/reverse/sum/product/fill/fill_keys/pad/chunk/column/diff/intersect(+_key/_assoc)/push/pop/shift/unshift/key_first/key_last/is_list`, `sort/rsort/usort/uasort/uksort/ksort/krsort/asort/arsort` (stable since 8.0, flags subset), `range`, `compact`/`extract` (dynamic profile), `list`, `implode`/`explode`/`str_split`, `array_key_exists`, `iterator_to_array`, `current/key/next/reset/end/prev` (the internal pointer is a per-array-value position in the cell content) | 900 |\\\\n   326\\\\t| Strings (byte strings) | `strlen`, `substr`, `strpos/stripos/strrpos`, `str_replace/str_ireplace`, `str_contains/starts_with/ends_with`, `trim/ltrim/rtrim`, `strtolower/strtoupper/ucfirst/ucwords/lcfirst` (ASCII, PHP 8 locale-insensitive), `str_repeat/str_pad/strrev/strcmp/strcasecmp/strncmp/strstr/strrchr/substr_count/wordwrap/nl2br/htmlspecialchars/html_entity_decode (basic)/addslashes/stripslashes/chunk_split`, `sprintf/printf/vsprintf/number_format`, `ord/chr/bin2hex/hex2bin/dechex/hexdec/decbin/bindec/octdec/decoct/base_convert`, `md5/sha1/crc32/hash('sha256')` via `data`/BLAKE3-era pure kernels only if present, else refused, `json_encode/json_decode` (flags subset, `JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR`, pretty print), `serialize/unserialize` deferred, `preg_*` refused | 900 |\\\\n   327\\\\t| Math | `abs/ceil/floor/round` (PHP's pre-rounding rule)/`intdiv/fmod/pow/sqrt/min/max/array_sum`, `PHP_INT_MAX/MIN/SIZE`, `PHP_FLOAT_*`, `M_PI`, `is_nan/is_finite/is_infinite`, `rand/mt_rand/random_int` as effects | 250 |\\\\n   328\\\\t| Functions and classes | call binding (positional, named, variadic, by-ref, defaults, type coercion/`TypeError`, `ArgumentCountError`), `func_get_args`, `call_user_func(_array)`, `is_callable`, `function_exists`, class table ops, `get_class`, `get_parent_class`, `method_exists`, `property_exists`, `class_exists`, `get_object_vars`, `spl_object_id`, visibility checks, magic dispatch, `Closure::bind/fromCallable/call`, enums `cases/from/tryFrom` | 700 |\\\\n   329\\\\t| Control and errors | handler stack (the Python pattern), `php/raise`, `finally`, escapes with levels, `Throwable` classes with `getMessage/getCode/getPrevious/getTrace (empty)/getLine (derived at the boundary)`, `set_error_handler/restore_error_handler/set_exception_handler/trigger_error/error_reporting`, warning emission `php/warn` | 350 |\\\\n   330\\\\t| Generators and iteration | C2 core under `php/`, `Iterator` protocol, `foreach` driver, `yield from` over arrays and generators | 300 |\\\\n   331\\\\t| Request and output | `$_*` construction, `php/echo`, `ob_*` stack, `header/headers_sent/http_response_code/setcookie`, `exit`, `php_sapi_name` (\\\\\\\"cli\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\"yin-http\\\\\\\" pinned), `getenv` from the record only, `PHP_EOL`, `PHP_VERSION` pinned, `error_log` as an effect | 300 |\\\\n   332\\\\t| Module runtime | `include/require/_once`, included-files dict, autoload class map, `define/constant/defined`, namespaces lookup | 250 |\\\\n   333\\\\t\\\\n   334\\\\tRefusal posture: a builtin outside the supported core is `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` at lowering (warning) and `Error: Call to undefined function` at run time; an extension surface is bound per ADR 0004 as its own slice with an effect schema and an interpreter; nothing is stubbed to return success.\\\\n   335\\\\t\\\\n   336\\\\t## B5. Value encoding and the paradigm rows finalized\\\\n   337\\\\t\\\\n   338\\\\t| PHP type | Representation |\\\\n   339\\\\t|---|---|\\\\n   340\\\\t| int | exact integer within `[-2^63, 2^63-1]` (C3 carriers; on JS a value past 2^53 is a `BigInt` carrier); overflow of an operation demotes to float |\\\\n   341\\\\t| float | Jing float64 content (carrier on JS); one NaN; `-0.0` preserved; `INF` |\\\\n   342\\\\t| string | **byte string**: a host string whose every char is one byte 0..255 (latin-1 carrier of the bytes); source literals contribute their UTF-8 bytes; `strlen` is bytes; output writes the bytes raw; `mb_*` is a separate slice over this representation. Owner decision B8.2 states the alternative. |\\\\n   343\\\\t| bool | host boolean |\\\\n   344\\\\t| null | `:php/null` |\\\\n   345\\\\t| array | persistent ordered-map value in the holder's cell or slot (B1) |\\\\n   346\\\\t| object | cell ref (handle); `clone` allocates a fresh cell |\\\\n   347\\\\t| reference | `{:php/ref c}` marker in a variable cell, array slot or property slot |\\\\n   348\\\\t| closure | object cell of class `Closure` holding the code closure, bound `$this`, scope class and `use`d values or markers |\\\\n   349\\\\t| enum case | singleton object cell per case |\\\\n   350\\\\t| resource | opaque handle data from a bound surface (`{:php/resource kind id}`), none in Phase 3 |\\\\n   351\\\\t| callable | string, `[class-or-obj, name]` array, or `Closure`; resolved at call |\\\\n   352\\\\t\\\\n   353\\\\t```text\\\\n   354\\\\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------+------------+\\\\n   355\\\\t| Paradigm                   | Universal AST target                             | Reference  |\\\\n   356\\\\t+============================+==================================================+============+\\\\n   357\\\\t| Value-copy ordered maps    | Arrays are persistent ordered-map values in      | PHP        |\\\\n   358\\\\t| with reference slots and   | cells (O(1) copy); references are markers in     |            |\\\\n   359\\\\t| request scope (new row,    | slots; objects are cell handles; locals are      |            |\\\\n   360\\\\t| finalizing D5)             | cells, dynamic-scope functions a heap symbol     |            |\\\\n   361\\\\t|                            | table; the global scope is the $GLOBALS dict; a  |            |\\\\n   362\\\\t|                            | request is one task reading one request record   |            |\\\\n   363\\\\t|                            | and appending ordered output records; warnings   |            |\\\\n   364\\\\t|                            | are diagnostic records, fatals are throws        |            |\\\\n   365\\\\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------+------------+\\\\n   366\\\\t| PHP number model           | int = exact integer bounded at 2^63 with overflow|            |\\\\n   367\\\\t|                            | to float (detected by exact promotion, demoted   |            |\\\\n   368\\\\t|                            | by rule); float = float64 content (carrier on    |            |\\\\n   369\\\\t|                            | JS); echo at precision 14, var_dump shortest;    |            |\\\\n   370\\\\t|                            | array keys coerce int-like strings and floats to |            |\\\\n   371\\\\t|                            | int                                              |            |\\\\n   372\\\\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------+------------+\\\\n   373\\\\t| Class-based OO (existing   | Class descriptors in cells, traits copied at     | PHP (with  |\\\\n   374\\\\t| row, PHP entry qualified)  | declaration, interfaces as dispatch contracts,   | Java,      |\\\\n   375\\\\t|                            | runtime visibility against a class context       | Python)    |\\\\n   376\\\\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------------+------------+\\\\n   377\\\\t```\\\\n   378\\\\t\\\\n   379\\\\t## B6. include/require over the linker, safepoints, diagnostics, the corpus\\\\n   380\\\\t\\\\n   381\\\\t- **Units and names**: a PHP file compiled as unit `src/lib/util.php` becomes linker module `phpm.src$lib$util` (injective mangling of the normalized relative path; `/` and `.` to `$`-escapes); shape as Python's: `(do (require 'php) (yin/def spec {:path \\\\\\\"src/lib/util.php\\\\\\\" :strict-types 0}) (yin/def body (fn [%scope %ctx] ...)))`. `include 'x.php'` with a **literal** path (after constant folding of `__DIR__ . '/x.php'`, which the lowering performs since `__DIR__` is the unit's declared path, not a filesystem fact) lowers to the I4-a statement-time delivery thunk; the body runs in the **including scope** (passing the including scope's symbol table, which is why an including function is on the dynamic profile; at top level it is `$GLOBALS`); the body's `return` value is the expression's value, else `1`. `_once` consults the included-files dict. A missing `include` is `Warning` plus `false`; a missing `require` is `Error` (PHP 8: `Error`, fatal). Computed paths are a diagnostic (ruling 10's literal-name restriction; a published literal path map can later interpret them). Conditional declarations inside included files execute in place, as PHP does. Cycles of `include` are a runtime matter (the included-files dict), not a linker cycle: static `include` edges are pinned in `:requires` only for delivery, and SCC publication handles mutual pins. **Autoload**: `spl_autoload_register` with a guest callable is supported only when the composition also publishes a literal **class map** (class name to unit) as part of the unit set; the autoloader then runs on a class miss and may `require` only literal paths in that map. Composer's generated class map is admissible as data; its filesystem resolution is not.\\\\n   382\\\\t- **Namespaces** are compile-time; nothing links per namespace.\\\\n   383\\\\t- **Safepoints**: `:loop` and `:call` for signals (`pcntl_signal` handlers run at hooks via `stream/poll!` on a signal stream, `pcntl_async_signals` is the default and only mode) and for recursion depth if a composition wants a bound (PHP has none; default off); `:line` under a ticks profile for `declare(ticks=N)` and `register_tick_function`. `max_execution_time` and `set_time_limit` are wall-clock in PHP, so nondeterministic: the profile offers a deterministic **safepoint-count budget** instead, raising the fatal with PHP's text; a recorded departure. No thread switches: PHP is single-threaded; one request is one task.\\\\n   384\\\\t- **Diagnostics**: compile-time `:yang.php/syntax`, `:yang.php/unsupported`, `:yang.php/not-php`, `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` (warning), `:yang.php/compile-error` for PHP's compile-time fatals (redeclared function in one unit, `break 0`, duplicate parameter, `$this` reassignment); runtime guest warnings on the guest-diagnostics stream; fatals as `Error` throws; uncaught text pinned.\\\\n   385\\\\t- **Differential corpus**: pinned PHP 8.3.x CLI with the pinned ini; stdout plus the diagnostics stream rendered in PHP's `Warning: ... in <unit> on line N` form with the path replaced by the unit name and the line derived from the side table (owner decision 2 of 8.5.1 reused) compared against PHP's stderr with paths normalized. Groups: juggling (every `==` pair of the PHP 8 table, numeric strings, arithmetic warnings/`TypeError`), arrays (key coercion, order, next index after unset, copy-on-write observable through references, nested writes, `foreach` by reference pitfalls, sort stability), references (`&` in all five positions, `global`, `static`), strings (bytes, interpolation forms, heredoc indentation, `precision=14` output, `var_dump` text), functions (named args, by-ref, defaults, variadics, type coercion vs `strict_types`), classes (traits precedence, visibility, static/late static binding, magic methods, readonly errors, enums, `match`), exceptions (finally ordering, multi-catch, `Error` hierarchy), generators, request (superglobals from a fixture record, headers after output warning, `ob_*`), inclusion (`_once`, return values, scope sharing, missing include warning vs require error), safepoints (ticks counting, signal at a hook).\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ncollab/yang-python/1792200000000-reviewer-ts-php-designs.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:39:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_19\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n 'float-digits|defn.*float' src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc; rg -n 'string|utf|surrogate|UTF' src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc | head -45; rg -n 'binders|:lambda|params|:variable' src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc | head -40; sed -n '2155,2291p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc; rg -n 'jobs|JavaScript|completion|shared|atomic|cell/swap' docs/design/yang.antlr.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"52:     printer. `float-digits` answers `[digits exp10]` for a finite\\\\n117:   `float-digits` and `decimal->float`, and `max-digits`, every version 3\\\\n434:(defn- ratio->float\\\\n466:(defn- int-to-float\\\\n481:(defn- float!\\\\n507:(defn- int-compare-float\\\\n526:(defn- int-from-float\\\\n652:  \\\\\\\"10^0 to 10^400 as big integers: every power `float-digits` needs.\\\\\\\"\\\\n683:(defn- float-ratio\\\\n721:(defn- int-float-digits\\\\n723:  (let [v (float! 'float-digits 0 f)]\\\\n725:      (wrong-type! 'float-digits 0 :finite-nonzero-float))\\\\n769:(defn- int-decimal->float\\\\n854:   ['float-digits [1] int-float-digits]\\\\n34:   stringref and date tags, with-meta, a dropped trailing index frame, and\\\\n39:   `:unpaired-surrogate`, ...); `refusal` reads it.\\\\n113:  \\\\\\\"An exact host big integer from a host integer or a decimal string.\\\\n119:                 (string? x) (BigInt.parse x)\\\\n125:                (string? x) (BigInteger. ^String x)\\\\n293:  \\\\\\\"A string naming the exact bytes bs[start, end), for duplicate checks.\\\\\\\"\\\\n351:     ;; a string or a bare Number that lost the float's kind. String\\\\n523:     \\\\\\\"The value of a short lowercase hex string.\\\\\\\"\\\\n565:   string. Every host accepts exactly the exponents in\\\\n709:  \\\\\\\"A host-independent value key of an exact triple: strings, so equal\\\\n793:  \\\\\\\"Portable decoded equality: numbers by num=, byte strings by content,\\\\n861:   denominator. Integer width is not identity. Built from strings and\\\\n884:   their kind-strict identity, byte strings by content, identifiers by their\\\\n939:  \\\\\\\"s itself, after refusing any unpaired UTF-16 surrogate.\\\\\\\"\\\\n949:              (refuse :unpaired-surrogate\\\\n950:                      (str \\\\\\\"unpaired high surrogate at \\\\\\\" i)))\\\\n952:            (refuse :unpaired-surrogate (str \\\\\\\"unpaired low surrogate at \\\\\\\" i))\\\\n1120:    (string? x) (do (deep! d :unsupported-value) (wire/text (check-text x)))\\\\n1126:                               (wire/byte-string (copy-range x 0 (blen x))))\\\\n1142:   values, unpaired surrogates, nesting deeper than max-depth, and\\\\n1239:(defn- utf8\\\\n1240:  \\\\\\\"Strict UTF-8 decode of bs[start, start+len).\\\\\\\"\\\\n1256:                          (refuse :invalid-utf8 (str e))))))))\\\\n1258:            (str (.decode (-> StandardCharsets/UTF_8\\\\n1264:              (refuse :invalid-utf8 (.getMessage e))))\\\\n1266:             (.decode (js/TextDecoder. \\\\\\\"utf-8\\\\\\\"\\\\n1270:               (refuse :invalid-utf8 (str e))))))\\\\n1330:                                      (utf8 bs cpos n))))))))\\\\n1334:                (if (= 2 major) (copy-range bs pos (+ pos n)) (utf8 bs pos n))\\\\n1498:                          \\\\\\\"bignum payload is not a byte string\\\\\\\"))\\\\n1530:                         \\\\\\\"tag 27 payload is not [name-string payload]\\\\\\\"))\\\\n1542:   interfaces). Returned byte strings are fresh copies.\\\\\\\"\\\\n1556:   these bytes. Returned byte strings are fresh copies.\\\\\\\"\\\\n49:    :lambda [[3 (get-attr eid :yin/body)]]\\\\n172:             (= :variable (:type operator))\\\\n203:    (if (and (= :application (:type node)) (= :lambda (:type (:operator node))))\\\\n(defn- module-tree\\\\n  \\\\\\\"A wide application: all definitions remain at module level.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [operands]\\\\n  (u/mark-tails\\\\n    (apply u/app (u/lam (mapv #(symbol (str \\\\\\\"%d\\\\\\\" %)) (range (count operands)))\\\\n                        (u/lit nil)) operands)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def ^:private initializing-key :yang.python.antlr/initializing)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn- cyclic-import-from\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Preserve IMPORT_FROM's attribute/submodule fallback, specializing its\\\\n   failure only while the target's task-local module object is initializing.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [m n]\\\\n  (u/let1 '%from-module m\\\\n          (u/let1 '%from-name n\\\\n                  (u/let1 '%from-result (app* 'cell/new none)\\\\n                          (app* 'py/try\\\\n                                (u/lam [] (app* 'cell/set! (u/v '%from-result)\\\\n                                                (app* 'py/import-from (u/v '%from-module) (u/v '%from-name))))\\\\n                                (u/lam ['%from-error]\\\\n                                       (u/if-node\\\\n                                         (app* 'get (app* 'cell/get (u/v '%from-module))\\\\n                                               (u/lit initializing-key) (u/lit false))\\\\n                                         (app* 'py/import-fail\\\\n                                               (app* 'py/str\\\\n                                                     (app* 'data/str-concat\\\\n                                                           (u/lit \\\\\\\"cannot import name '\\\\\\\")\\\\n                                                           (app* 'get (u/v '%from-name) (u/lit :py/str))\\\\n                                                           (u/lit \\\\\\\"' from partially initialized module '\\\\\\\")\\\\n                                                           (app* 'get (app* 'py/lookup-attr (u/v '%from-module)\\\\n                                                                            (u/lit \\\\\\\"__name__\\\\\\\")) (u/lit :py/str))\\\\n                                                           (u/lit \\\\\\\"' (most likely due to a circular import)\\\\\\\"))))\\\\n                                         (app* 'py/raise (u/v '%from-error))))\\\\n                                (u/lam [] (app* 'cell/get (u/v '%from-result))))))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn scc-module-specs\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Canonical I5 construction: sorted members, indexed bare exports\\\\n   m0-spec/m0-body, etc.; one pyscc.<mangled-members> bundle followed by\\\\n   aliases in member order. Internal deliveries read those exports without\\\\n   requiring aliases. Only py and outgoing imports are pinned by the bundle.\\\\n   Alias :requires is filled with the bundle address after publication.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [registry units py-address deps]\\\\n  (doseq [{:keys [name]} units]\\\\n    (validate-module-name! name))\\\\n  (let [units (vec (sort-by :name units))\\\\n        deps (apply dissoc deps (map :name units))\\\\n        bundle-name (symbol (str \\\\\\\"pyscc.\\\\\\\" (str/join \\\\\\\"$$\\\\\\\" (map #(str/replace (:name %) \\\\\\\".\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"$\\\\\\\") units))))\\\\n        keys-for (into {} (map-indexed\\\\n                            (fn [i unit]\\\\n                              [(:name unit) [(symbol (str \\\\\\\"m\\\\\\\" i \\\\\\\"-spec\\\\\\\"))\\\\n                                             (symbol (str \\\\\\\"m\\\\\\\" i \\\\\\\"-body\\\\\\\"))]]) units))\\\\n        units-by-name (into {} (map (fn [u] [(:name u) u]) units))\\\\n        internal-names (into {} (map (fn [nm] [(module-symbol nm) nm])) (keys keys-for))\\\\n        internal (set (keys internal-names))\\\\n        rewrite (fn [node]\\\\n                  (cond\\\\n                    (and (= :variable (:type node))\\\\n                         (symbol? (:name node))\\\\n                         (some? (namespace (:name node)))\\\\n                         (contains? internal (symbol (namespace (:name node))))\\\\n                         (= \\\\\\\"spec\\\\\\\" (name (:name node))))\\\\n                    (let [nm (get internal-names (symbol (namespace (:name node))))\\\\n                          u (get units-by-name nm)]\\\\n                      (u/lit {:name nm, :package? (boolean (:package? u))}))\\\\n                    (and (= :variable (:type node))\\\\n                         (symbol? (:name node))\\\\n                         (some? (namespace (:name node)))\\\\n                         (contains? internal (symbol (namespace (:name node))))\\\\n                         (= \\\\\\\"body\\\\\\\" (name (:name node))))\\\\n                    (let [nm (get internal-names (symbol (namespace (:name node))))\\\\n                          [_ body-key] (get keys-for nm)]\\\\n                      (u/v body-key))\\\\n                    (and (= :application (:type node))\\\\n                         (= 'try-require (get-in node [:operator :name]))\\\\n                         (contains? internal (get-in node [:operands 0 :value])))\\\\n                    (u/lit {:status :ok})\\\\n                    (and (= :application (:type node))\\\\n                         (= 'py/import-from (get-in node [:operator :name])))\\\\n                    (apply cyclic-import-from (:operands node))\\\\n                    :else node))\\\\n        wrapped-bodies\\\\n        (mapv (fn [{:keys [name packet package?]}]\\\\n                (let [unit {:name name, :package? (boolean package?)}\\\\n                      body (walk/postwalk rewrite (lower-module-body packet unit))\\\\n                      flag (fn [v]\\\\n                             (app* 'cell/set! (u/v '%module)\\\\n                                   (app* 'assoc (app* 'cell/get (u/v '%module))\\\\n                                         (u/lit initializing-key) (u/lit v))))]\\\\n                  (u/lam [globals-sym globals-fn-sym]\\\\n                         (u/let1 '%module (app* 'py/modules-ref (u/lit {:py/str name}))\\\\n                                 (u/then (flag true)\\\\n                                         (app* 'py/try-finally (u/lam [] body)\\\\n                                               (u/lam [u/discard] (flag false))))))))\\\\n              units)\\\\n        spec-defs\\\\n        (mapcat (fn [{:keys [name package?]}]\\\\n                  (let [[spec-key _] (get keys-for name)\\\\n                        unit {:name name, :package? (boolean package?)}]\\\\n                    [(u/def! spec-key (u/lit unit))]))\\\\n                units)\\\\n        body-defs\\\\n        (map (fn [{:keys [name]} body]\\\\n               (let [[_ body-key] (get keys-for name)]\\\\n                 (u/def! body-key body)))\\\\n             units wrapped-bodies)\\\\n        ;; The linker discharges body reads only when their definitions\\\\n        ;; precede every module-level application site. Install the pure\\\\n        ;; sibling bindings before require; defining the lambdas runs no py.\\\\n        ast (module-tree (concat spec-defs\\\\n                                 body-defs\\\\n                                 [(require-node prelude/module-name)]))\\\\n        exports (set (mapcat val keys-for))\\\\n        requires (into {prelude/module-name py-address}\\\\n                       (map (fn [[n a]] [(module-symbol n) a])) deps)\\\\n        free (remove (conj (prelude/defined-keys ast) 'yin/def) (prelude/free-names ast))\\\\n        bundle {:name bundle-name, :ast ast, :exports exports, :requires requires,\\\\n                :primitives (into {} (keep (partial declare-free-name registry (set (keys requires))))\\\\n                                  (sort-by str free))}]\\\\n    (into [bundle]\\\\n          (map (fn [{:keys [name]}]\\\\n                 (let [[sk bk] (get keys-for name)]\\\\n                   {:name (module-symbol name), :exports module-exports,\\\\n                    :primitives {'require (vm/profile-of vm/primitives 'require)},\\\\n                    :ast (module-tree\\\\n                           [(require-node bundle-name)\\\\n                            (u/def! 'spec (u/v (symbol (str bundle-name) (str sk))))\\\\n                            (u/def! 'body (u/v (symbol (str bundle-name) (str bk))))])})))\\\\n          units)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\n;; The lowering stage\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\n\\\\n12:section 8.5.5 (`1f8b7e37`, with the JavaScript carrier's coercion refusal in\\\\n21:only), and every phase after Phase 1 (the JavaScript pilot, Java, PHP, the\\\\n105:language named below (Java, Python, PHP, JavaScript, Go, Rust, Clojure,\\\\n122:runtime prelude. Java, Python, PHP, and JavaScript are reference\\\\n135:Content puts and fetched bytes pass the shared `dao.jing/accept-bytes!`\\\\n213:- JavaScript is described as future work in the Yang documentation; no\\\\n265:- **No implicit control flow:** admission, parse completion, retries,\\\\n270:- **No shared mutable state:** compiler state is immutable and threaded\\\\n326:- Generated JVM classes, JavaScript modules, or Dart libraries.\\\\n497:Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, and Dart. Target feature parity is not\\\\n512:| Node / CLJS   | Generated JavaScript parser   | Local sidecar or remote  |\\\\n551:| CLJS      | -Dlanguage=JavaScript  | antlr4 (npm)                     |\\\\n581:Generated recognizers may use shared caches. The implementation must\\\\n587:Read-only generated tables may be shared. No semantic state may depend\\\\n612:- The host completion handler deposits data and returns.\\\\n675:- A shared REPL stream remains open between submissions.\\\\n756:- A completion record identifying the complete packet.\\\\n887:For large artifacts, stage chunks with a manifest and completion record.\\\\n999:JavaScript calls are not automatically Yin macros.\\\\n1014:Free-name queries must remain root- and occurrence-sco